      "number": 1,
      "status": "accepted",
      "explanation": "Replace the per\u2011iteration copy\u2011and\u2011sum with an incremental sum. The original code copies the whole vector for each of the 16 iterations (via sum_copy) and then recomputes the total with std::accumulate, costing O(n) work per iteration. Because the loop only adds a small value i to a single element, the overall sum can be updated by adding i to a running sum. This preserves the exact numeric result (kernel is never called with n==0) while eliminating the expensive copies and repeated accumulation, yielding a faster O(n+16) algorithm.",
      "model_call": {
        "settings": {
          "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b",
          "temperature": 0.2,
          "top_p": 1,
